{"kind":"request","text":"Hugh approves the JSON-output discussion and requests a full detailed specification from planner for a GLOBAL --json flag affecting ALL CLI commands. This is design/specification work, not implementation before the demo. Start from discussion report 5784eaed and current CLI source: packages/cli/src/line.ts accepts no json flag, Outcome in commands.ts contains only code/lines, and main.ts prints prose. Define typed command results first, with text and JSON renderings from the same data; do not wrap existing prose lines and call that structured output. Cover every command and subcommand, including install variants, claim, invite, join, acts, act, log, show, verify/verify --all, remote, clone, edit, propose, merge, issue variants and issues. Cover fresh, resumed, partially complete, refused, unavailable, mismatch, unknown, unsupported, usage, unexpected-error and successful outcomes where each applies. Specify global-flag placement, parser behavior and interaction with existing flags; one stable versioned schema and exact per-command payloads; stdout/stderr/progress and child-process output rules; exit status; pretty/compact behavior; bounded/streamed large histories and whether a separate JSON-lines mode is needed; public compatibility guarantees and schema evolution. Keep close to public native structures: full ScopeRef/incarnation, definition pins, KeyId/MemberRef/standing, separate read heads, Read/Answer/Receipt/replay data as appropriate. Preserve acceptance versus observation/publication and unknown-versus-refused distinctions; never imply an aggregate read is atomic or that a catalog listing guarantees admission. For acts, use a map by kind with native step/on/grant, complete field constraints/defaults/nested types, nonempty also and other required inputs such as presents; default catalog omits rule/effect programs and full detail remains accessible. The C1 source-only measurement was 13 non-genesis schemas: 2705 compact bytes versus 8436 bytes of full act forms, excluding common metadata; use this as evidence, not a universal size claim. Enumerate safe serialization boundaries, including commands whose native/public entries or intentional output contain invitation material; never dump private Context/Store/key/session/provider credentials or claim that a global mode sanitizes history it does not. Specify existing public-output compatibility and a command-by-command verification matrix with meaningful invariants and ownership. State remaining decisions explicitly, avoiding premature implementation choices. Put the complete spec in the repository’s established design documentation, seek its normal review, and derive separately scoped implementation requests afterward. No source implementation, package publication, live acts, deployment or JSON migration before the demo.","body":{"conditions":"Write and review a complete design specification for a global --json flag covering every CLI command, with exact schemas, command-by-command mapping, output/error/stream rules, compatibility and acceptance criteria. Specification only before the demo; no implementation before the demo. File implementation work only after the specification is reviewed and the demo constraint permits it.","target_head":"013fac7a5c0d65affda51198ae251acb19b6b765","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}